2026-09-27T03:28:08.7651578Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7652023Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7652420Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7653306Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7654069Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7654145Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7654322Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7654582Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7654828Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7654931Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7655122Z ================
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7655232Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7655370Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7655692Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7655878Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7655984Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7656229Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7656392Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7656519Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7656869Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7657184Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7657773Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7658219Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7658326Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7658703Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7659254Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7659501Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7659763Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7660115Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7660193Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7660382Z ========
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7660481Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7661900Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7663025Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7663228Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7663651Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7664061Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7664564Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7665053Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7665433Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7665662Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7666082Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7666336Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7666480Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7667387Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7668456Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7669013Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7669753Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:28:08.7669941Z 
